================================================================================
Authoritative sources (REFERENCED — read as evidence, not copied)
================================================================================

Under GEML's clean-room rules, the pure-EML construction is implemented from
public authoritative sources, independently expressed in GEML's own IR. No code
from these sources is vendored or copied. Provenance and approval metadata for
each is recorded in docs/specs/EML_SOURCE_LEDGER.md.

  - Andrzej Odrzywołek, "All elementary functions from a single operator."
    arXiv:2603.21852. https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.21852
      The single-operator eml(x, y) = exp(x) - ln(y) construction that GEML is
      built on. Used as a scientific source (grammar, construction coverage,
      domain caveats) — not as code.

  - Official EML reference compiler: eml_compiler_v4.py in
    VA00/SymbolicRegressionPackage, commit b3da148261199b46247306dfd92068f589778260.
    https://github.com/VA00/SymbolicRegressionPackage
      Authoritative implementation evidence for operator constructions and
      domain behavior. Read for corroboration only; no upstream code is copied.
      GEML's formulas are independently expressed and checked against exact
      offline fingerprints.

The v0 GEML prototype is historical motivation only and is explicitly NOT a
source: its code, tests, and
schemas are forbidden implementation inputs under docs/CLEANROOM_RULES.md.
